      "title": "Every lexical criterion labels an invented paraphrase as a quoted expression from the transcript",
      "evidence": "The criterion says 'expresiones realmente presentes' and places detail inside guillemets, but the quoted detail is absent from the associated transcript in 40/40 samples. Examples include Set 21 Band 5.5 «the monthly clean-up», Set 21 Band 9 «the shift from physical repair to stronger neighbourhood…», and Set 40 Band 9 «the move from editing survey wording to clarifying its purpose». Across verdict plus criteria, 280/320 quoted fragments are traceable and these 40 are not.",
      "impact": "The feedback presents paraphrase as verbatim evidence. This violates the requested traceability rule and can teach learners to trust a lexical observation that was not actually made on the sample.",
      "requiredRemediation": "Select the lexical quotation directly from the transcript, or explicitly label the detail as a reviewer paraphrase without guillemets or a claim that it is present. Add a test that normalizes ellipsis and asserts every quoted fragment is a transcript substring. Any source change invalidates this report hash."
